er operating revenues of $81.0 million for VALARIS 247 and VALARIS DPS-1, which completed their contracts and were sold since the end of the prior year period. For the remaining fleet, we had a net decrease of $181.4 million from fewer operating days, largely attributable to certain floaters which were either preparing for contracts or warm stacked between contracts during the current year period. These decreases were partially offset by a net increase of $37.3 million from higher average daily revenues as a result of various rigs working under higher day rate contracts compared to the prior year period.\n"}
